AMSAT Satellite Status Page and API
Site: https://status.amsat.org
API: https://status.amsat.org/api/v1/ (versions index: https://status.amsat.org/api/)

CHANGE LOG:
2022-07-19: Status page and API shifted to open development. Initial commit to AMSAT Gitlab instance.
2023-04-21: Consolidate config.php references to single config file (in root folder).
2026-03-25: Update color pallete to IBM Colorblind Safe Palette
2026-05-20: Security fixes related to database interactions
2026-05-23:
    - Removed "ISS Crew Active" status option. (Issue #13)
    - Updated status table legend, tool tip, and report types to be in sync
2026-06-17:
    - Migrated repository from GitLab to GitHub
    - CI pipeline ported to GitHub Actions (PHPUnit + Playwright test suites, build artifact)
2026-06-18:
    - Restructured the repo into versioned frontend/v1/ and api/v1/
      directories, each with its own Dockerfile, plus db/ for schema and
      seed data, and a three-service docker-compose.yml (frontend, api,
      db). No functional changes. (PR #6, commit 0c0abe1)
    - Moved the test configs into tests/ and gave each Docker build
      context its own .dockerignore. (PR #7, commit 2b5f3bc)
    - Added a docker-compose smoke-test CI job that builds the real
      stack and checks the frontend, API health and seeded data.
      (PR #8, commit 7bfd543)
    - Added Traefik routing labels for status.amsat.org, with /api routed
      to the API container. (PR #9, commit 39c3843)
2026-07-17:
    - Removed the completed survey banner from the status page.
      (PR #11, commit f03835c)
2026-07-27:
    - Added the CD pipeline: CI gate, path-filtered image build, push to
      Azure Container Registry, then configure and deploy to azure193.
      (PR #12, commit 6070266)
    - Upgraded MariaDB from 11.4 to the 12.3 LTS. (PR #16, commit 9971d1a)
2026-07-28:
    - Fixed the production DB healthcheck on azure193 (now uses a TCP
      loopback check), and enabled MARIADB_AUTO_UPGRADE for future
      version bumps. (PR #17, commit 497d43c)
2026-07-31:
    - The Donate button now links to the AMSAT General Fund donations
      page instead of the old PayPal campaign. (PR #13, commit d915c24)
    - Added a Traefik restart after each deploy to work around
      intermittent 504s (PR #18, commit 0d1880b). It was removed the same
      day once the real cause was fixed in amsat-it-infra: Traefik was
      routing to the wrong Docker network. (PR #19, commit 58b9cf2)
2026-08-01:
    - Added deploy-time versioning (Issue #20): frontend footer now shows the
      last-deployed date/time and short commit SHA; API responses carry
      X-AMSAT-API-Commit / X-AMSAT-API-Deployed-At headers. Values are
      generated by the CD pipeline at deploy time from github.sha and the
      runner's clock, not stored as a new repo variable.
    - Established the CHANGELOG-update convention for AI agent work,
      documented in docs/agents/changelog-convention.md (not CI-enforced —
      see that doc for why), and refreshed the docs/agents/ knowledge
      bundle, which had gone stale since CD shipped.
    - Commit: ed6fb69
    - Consolidated SITE_URL handling and fixed a trailing-slash bug that
      produced double-slash links on the admin pages. CI now checks that
      API self-links match the production URL exactly.
      (PR #21, commit 539dcba)
2026-08-02:
    - The "Reports From" list now scrolls instead of stretching the page,
      and is sorted by most recent report. (Issue #27, PR #28,
      commit 0993ef4)
2026-08-23:
    - Added a reusable, file-toggled site announcement banner. A banner is
      live if and only if frontend/v1/content/banner.md exists and is
      non-empty (gitignored, host-edited directly, never committed; a
      tracked frontend/v1/content/banner.md.example ships as the template).
      Rendered by a new dedicated endpoint (frontend/v1/banner.php) as a
      complete, self-contained HTML document -- Markdown via a vendored
      copy of Parsedown (frontend/v1/lib/Parsedown.php, MIT, this app's
      first third-party runtime PHP dependency; vendored as a single file
      rather than composer-installed, since this repo's Docker builds
      don't run `composer install`), raw HTML passthrough intentionally
      unsanitized (content is host-edited only, never user- or API-
      submitted), tag-balanced via DOMDocument, every link forced to
      target="_blank" rel="noopener". index.php embeds it via <iframe>
      for genuine DOM isolation -- malformed banner markup structurally
      cannot affect the parent page -- only when a banner is actually
      active, auto-resized to fit via postMessage. Also added a CHANGELOG
      link to the existing footer, next to the deploy commit info; this
      file isn't served anywhere in-app, so it links to the GitHub blob
      view. (PR #33, commit c9b310a)
2026-08-24:
    - Fixed CD so it ships content/banner.md.example to the deploy host
      and creates the content/ directory. (PR #34, commit 6cdc23c)
2026-10-24:
    - Security: rebuilt the frontend and API images on PHP 8.5.12 for
      CVE-2026-109618 / CVE-2026-109619 (unauthenticated RCE, fixed in
      8.5.12). Base images are now pinned to php:8.5-apache instead of a
      floating php:apache, so patch releases still come in but a major
      bump can't land by surprise. Builds now always re-pull the base
      image. (PR #36, commit 20380db)
    - CD can now be run manually ("Run workflow"). A manual run rebuilds
      both images from scratch, without cache, and deploys from main.
      (PRs #35 and #36, commits 1880c1f and 20380db)
2026-10-27:
    - API root (/api/v1/) now returns a machine-readable JSON discovery
      document instead of a plain-text listing: API name and version,
      links to the prose overview, Swagger UI, OpenAPI document, health
      check and CHANGELOG, and the full endpoint list (method, path,
      absolute URL, summary, legacy/deprecated flags). The endpoint list
      is generated from openapi.json at request time, so it can't drift
      from the documented contract. Uses the standard JSON envelope
      (data, CORS, X-AMSAT-API-* headers). Content-Type changes from
      text/plain to application/json; no known consumer parses the old
      text output. (Issue #38, PR #39, commit 9701584)
    - Added an /api front door (api/index.php): a machine-readable JSON
      index of API versions (currently just v1, status "current") with
      each version's base URL, Swagger UI and OpenAPI links. Previously
      /api returned 403. It is deliberately not an alias for the latest
      version -- it points at versioned base URLs and never serves data
      endpoints, so clients pinned to /api/v1/ are never moved silently.
      To ship it in the API image, the build context moved from ./api/v1
      to ./api (Dockerfile now api/Dockerfile, explicit COPYs so build
      files are no longer in the web root; cd.yml contexts and path
      filter, and docker-compose.yml, updated to match). (Issue #38,
      PR #40)
    - CHANGELOG convention (docs/agents/changelog-convention.md): entries
      now reference the PR number, which is required, instead of a
      commit SHA. Squash merges create the final SHA only at merge time,
      so it can't be recorded when the entry is written, and a branch
      SHA doesn't end up on main. Every PR gets an entry unless
      explicitly told otherwise. (PR #41)
2026-10-29:
    - The project now has a license: source code is Apache-2.0 (new
      LICENSE file; composer.json / package.json no longer say
      "proprietary" / "UNLICENSED"), and report data served by the API
      is CC BY 4.0 with attribution. Added API usage guidelines to the
      overview page (overview.php#usage): identify clients with a
      descriptive User-Agent, poll no more than every 5 minutes, submit
      only real observations by the operator whose callsign the report
      carries (apps submitting on their users' behalf are welcome; imports
      from other networks or automated reports need agreement first),
      don't use report data to track operators, and how breaking changes
      are announced. The OpenAPI
      document now carries license, contact and termsOfService. README
      and this file's header point at status.amsat.org. (Issue #42,
      PR #43)
